@startuml
title Smart Product Framework - End-to-End Sequence Flow

actor "Product Provider" as PProvider
actor Client
participant "Frontend / dApp" as Frontend
participant "TextResource\n(product terms template)\n----\nITextResource" as ProductTermsTemplate
participant "TextResource\n(product documentation template)\n----\nITextResource" as ProductDocumentationTemplate
participant "ClientRegistry\n\n----\nIClientRegistry" as ClientRegistry
participant "BondProductRegistry\n----\nAbstractProductRegistry\n----\nIProductDefinitionRegistry" as Registry
participant "CurveIndications" as CurveRegistry
participant "ProductFactoryRegistry\n(generic)" as GenericFactory
participant "SimpleBondFactory\n(product-specific)" as ProductSpecificFactory
participant "SimpleBond\n(deployed product)" as Bond
participant "EvmXmlRenderer" as Renderer

== Initial Setup ==

PProvider -> ClientRegistry : deploy ClientRegistry(owner)
PProvider -> Registry : deploy BondProductRegistry(owner, clientRegistry)
PProvider -> GenericFactory : deploy ProductFactoryRegistry(owner, registry)
PProvider -> Registry : setProductFactory(factory)
Registry -> GenericFactory : productRegistryAddress()
GenericFactory --> Registry : registry (back-reference check)

== Register a Product Factory (here: SimpleBondFactory) ==

PProvider -> ProductSpecificFactory : deploy SimpleBondFactory(genericFactory)
PProvider -> GenericFactory : registerProductFactory(SIMPLE_BOND_TYPE, productSpecificFactory)
GenericFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : supportsInterface(IProductSpecificFactory)
ProductSpecificFactory --> GenericFactory : true
GenericFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : productTypeId()
ProductSpecificFactory --> GenericFactory : SIMPLE_BOND_TYPE (type match)
GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : store Active factory configuration
GenericFactory --> PProvider : ProductFactoryRegistered

note right of GenericFactory
The generic factory is the source of truth for:
productTypeId -> active product-specific factory.
end note

== Resource Publication ==

PProvider -> ProductTermsTemplate : deploy TextResource(owner, BOND_PRODUCT_TERMS_TEMPLATE_RESOURCE_TYPE,\n"application/xml", bytes(""), bytes32(0))
loop for every product terms template chunk
	PProvider -> ProductTermsTemplate : appendChunk(chunk)
end
PProvider -> ProductTermsTemplate : finalize(keccak256(content))
ProductTermsTemplate -> ProductTermsTemplate : read chunks + verify hash + lock resource
ProductTermsTemplate --> PProvider : finalized product terms template

PProvider -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : deploy TextResource(owner, BOND_PRODUCT_DOCUMENTATION_TEMPLATE_RESOURCE_TYPE,\n"application/xslt+xml", bytes(""), bytes32(0))
loop for every product documentation template chunk
	PProvider -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : appendChunk(chunk)
end
PProvider -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : finalize(keccak256(content))
ProductDocumentationTemplate -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : read chunks + verify hash + lock resource
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> PProvider : finalized product documentation template

note over ProductTermsTemplate, ProductDocumentationTemplate
TextResource also supports one-shot publication by passing
content and its expected hash to the constructor. DemoEndToEndWorkflow uses
the staged appendChunk + finalize workflow shown above.
end note

== Product Definition Publication ==

PProvider -> Registry : publishProductDefinition({name, {productTermsTemplate, productDocumentationTemplate, productTypeId}})

Registry -> ProductTermsTemplate : supportsInterface(ITextResource)
ProductTermsTemplate --> Registry : true
Registry -> ProductTermsTemplate : isFinalized()
ProductTermsTemplate --> Registry : true
Registry -> ProductTermsTemplate : resourceType()
ProductTermsTemplate --> Registry : BOND_PRODUCT_TERMS_TEMPLATE_RESOURCE_TYPE

Registry -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : supportsInterface(ITextResource)
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Registry : true
Registry -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : isFinalized()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Registry : true
Registry -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : resourceType()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Registry : BOND_PRODUCT_DOCUMENTATION_TEMPLATE_RESOURCE_TYPE

Registry -> Registry : productDefinitionId = keccak256(abi.encode(name, address(this)))
Registry -> Registry : store ProductDefinitionStorage\n(status = Active, version = 1)
Registry --> PProvider : ProductDefinitionPublished + StatePartUpdated

PProvider -> Registry : computeProductDefinitionId(name)
Registry --> PProvider : productDefinitionId\n(partId = uint256(productDefinitionId))

note over PProvider, Client
The registry's statePartXmlTemplate(partId) returns ProductDefinition
with ProductResources. ProductTermsTemplate and
ProductDocumentationTemplate each contain a parse="text" XInclude.
This remains a source preview:
evmstate bindings are returned as text and are not evaluated
against the registry.
end note

== Indication Publication and Assignment ==

PProvider -> CurveRegistry : deploy CurveIndications(owner)
PProvider -> CurveRegistry : publishCurveIndications(curveName, quotes[])
CurveRegistry -> CurveRegistry : curveId = keccak256(abi.encode(curveName, address(this)))
CurveRegistry -> CurveRegistry : store active quote board + touch indication version
CurveRegistry --> PProvider : IndicationPublished + StatePartUpdated
PProvider -> PProvider : derive indicationId / curveId

PProvider -> Registry : assignProductIndication(productDefinitionId, curveRegistry, indicationId)
Registry -> CurveRegistry : supportsInterface(IProductIndication)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : true
Registry -> CurveRegistry : indicationStatus(indicationId)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : Active
Registry -> CurveRegistry : indicationCategory()
CurveRegistry --> Registry : CURVE
Registry -> Registry : _isAcceptedIndication(productTypeId, CURVE) == true
Registry -> CurveRegistry : partIdForIndication(indicationId)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : indicationPartId
Registry -> Registry : store (curveRegistry, indicationId, partId)\nand increment product-definition version
Registry --> PProvider : ProductIndicationAssigned + StatePartUpdated

note right of Registry
Registry stores per productDefinitionId:
- productTermsTemplate + productDocumentationTemplate
- productTypeId
- (productIndication, indicationId, partId)

Assignment accepts Active or Suspended indications.
Current trade creation does not re-check indication liveness.
end note

== Client Registration ==

PProvider -> ClientRegistry : registerClient({client, lei})
ClientRegistry -> ClientRegistry : store status = Active
ClientRegistry --> PProvider : ClientRegistered + ClientStatusChanged

== Frontend Prepares Trade Request ==

Client -> Frontend : select product definition

Frontend -> Registry : productIndicationOfDefinition(productDefinitionId)
Registry --> Frontend : indicationContract, indicationId, partId

Frontend -> Renderer : render indication(contract, partId)
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : statePartXmlTemplate(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : lean XML template with\nevmstate:args="$partId" callbacks
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : indicationStatusByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : status
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : activeQuoteCountByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : quote count
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : activeQuotesByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : QuoteView[]
Renderer -> Renderer : expand quote rows and format fields
Renderer --> Frontend : curve indication XML

Frontend -> Registry : productTypeByDefinitionId(productDefinitionId)
Registry --> Frontend : productTypeId

Frontend -> GenericFactory : productFactoryOf(productTypeId)
GenericFactory --> Frontend : specific factory address

Frontend -> ProductSpecificFactory : productSpecificPayloadSchema()
ProductSpecificFactory --> Frontend : schema string
Frontend -> ProductSpecificFactory : productSpecificSchemaHash()
ProductSpecificFactory --> Frontend : schema hash

note right of Frontend
productSpecificPayloadSchema() is a concrete-factory helper;
it is not currently declared by IProductSpecificFactory.

SimpleBond payload fields:
- notional
- maturity
end note

Frontend -> Frontend : ABI-encode productSpecificPayload
Frontend -> Frontend : attach productSpecificSchemaHash

== Trade Request and Deployment ==

Client -> Frontend : submit trade request
Frontend -> Registry : createTradeRequest({productDefinitionId, schemaHash, payload})\n(client-signed transaction)

Registry -> Registry : require productFactory set
Registry -> Registry : load ProductDefinitionStorage(productDefinitionId)
Registry -> Registry : require product definition Active

Registry -> ClientRegistry : isEligibleClient(client, productDefinitionId)
ClientRegistry --> Registry : true

Registry -> GenericFactory : canDeployProduct(productTypeId)
GenericFactory --> Registry : true

Registry -> Registry : tradeId = keccak256(abi.encode(\nregistry, chainId, nonce, client, productDefinitionId))
Registry -> ProductTermsTemplate : contentHash()
ProductTermsTemplate --> Registry : productTermsTemplateContentHash
Registry -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : contentHash()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Registry : productDocumentationTemplateContentHash
Registry -> Registry : deploymentStateHash = keccak256(abi.encode(\ncommon state, resource addresses + hashes,\nschemaHash, keccak256(payload)))

Registry -> GenericFactory : deployProduct({common, schemaHash, payload})

GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : require msg.sender == productRegistryAddress
GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : load factory configuration for productTypeId
GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : require configuration Active
GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : require tradeId unused

GenericFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : deployProduct({common, schemaHash, payload})

ProductSpecificFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : require msg.sender == genericFactory
ProductSpecificFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : require schemaHash == productSpecificSchemaHash()
ProductSpecificFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : require common.productTypeId == productTypeId()

ProductSpecificFactory -> Bond : new SimpleBond(common, payload)
Bond -> Bond : store immutable common state
Bond -> Bond : productSpecificFactory = msg.sender (product-specific factory)
Bond -> Bond : status = Requested\n emit TradeStatusChanged(Requested, Requested)
Bond -> Bond : _applyTerms(payload) -> decode + validate
Bond -> Bond : emit StateUpdated
Bond --> ProductSpecificFactory : product address

ProductSpecificFactory -> ProductSpecificFactory : isFactoryDeployedProduct[product] = true
ProductSpecificFactory --> GenericFactory : product

GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : productByTradeId[tradeId] = product
GenericFactory -> GenericFactory : emit ProductDeployed
GenericFactory --> Registry : product

Registry -> Registry : _productByTradeId[tradeId] = product
Registry -> Registry : emit TradeRequestCreated
Registry --> Frontend : transaction event contains tradeId + product
Frontend --> Client : product deployed (status Requested)

== Trade Lifecycle (incept / confirm) ==

opt client amends terms while Requested
	Client -> Frontend : update terms
	Frontend -> Bond : updateTerms(payload)\n(client-signed transaction)
	Bond -> Bond : require client + status Requested
	Bond -> Bond : _applyTerms(payload)
	Bond -> Bond : emit TermsUpdated + StateUpdated
	Bond --> Frontend : ok
end

PProvider -> Frontend : read current terms hash
Frontend -> Bond : currentTermsHash()
Bond --> Frontend : agreedTermsHash

PProvider -> Bond : inceptTrade(agreedTermsHash)
Bond -> Bond : require product provider + status Requested
Bond -> Bond : require agreedTermsHash == currentTermsHash()
Bond -> Bond : store agreedTermsHash\nstatus = Incepted
Bond -> Bond : emit TradeStatusChanged + TradeIncepted
Bond --> PProvider : ok

Client -> Bond : confirmTrade(agreedTermsHash)
Bond -> Bond : require client + status Incepted
Bond -> Bond : require agreedTermsHash == stored hash
Bond -> Bond : status = Active
Bond -> Bond : emit TradeStatusChanged + TradeConfirmed + TradeActivated
Bond -> Bond : _onActivated() (product-specific hook)
Bond --> Client : trade Active

== Product State Rendering and Documentation Generation ==

Client -> Frontend : open product
Frontend -> Renderer : render(product)

Renderer -> Bond : stateXmlTemplate()
Bond -> ProductTermsTemplate : web3Url()
ProductTermsTemplate --> Bond : canonical product terms template URL
Bond -> ProductTermsTemplate : contentHash()
ProductTermsTemplate --> Bond : product terms template integrity hash
Bond -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : web3Url()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Bond : canonical product documentation template URL
Bond -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : contentHash()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Bond : product documentation template integrity hash
Bond --> Renderer : SimpleBond state template with DeploymentState\nand ProductResources role wrappers containing both XIncludes

Renderer -> ProductTermsTemplate : content() via ProductTermsTemplate XInclude
ProductTermsTemplate --> Renderer : product terms template
Renderer -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : content() via ProductDocumentationTemplate XInclude
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Renderer : product documentation template

Renderer -> Renderer : resolve no-argument evmstate:call bindings\nagainst the deployed SimpleBond
Renderer -> Bond : productRegistry(), productSpecificFactory(),\ntradeId(), parties, definition data, tradeStatus(), ...
Bond --> Renderer : deployment and lifecycle values
Renderer -> Bond : notional()
Bond --> Renderer : value
Renderer -> Bond : maturity()
Bond --> Renderer : value

Renderer -> Renderer : identity-transform / serialize resolved product state
Renderer --> Frontend : resolved product state

Frontend -> ProductDocumentationTemplate : text()
ProductDocumentationTemplate --> Frontend : product documentation template
Frontend -> Frontend : apply product documentation template\nto resolved product state
Frontend --> Client : display rendered product documentation

note right of Renderer
EvmXmlRenderer resolves XIncludes and no-argument
evmstate bindings. During state-part rendering it also
supports one uint256 callback argument supplied as $partId.
It does not currently execute XSLT;
DemoEndToEndWorkflow applies the product documentation template separately.
end note

@enduml
